#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In this example, the vehicle is placed in a "virtual wind tunnel" which allows the aerodynamics behavior to be studied and verified.
#
#The effect of the trailer on the car is interpreted by calculating aero coefficients for the combined car with trailer, resolved at the aero reference point of the car. This calculation assumes that the car and trailer are rigidly connected together, which is not true in general (the ball hitch does not transfer moments). However, vehicles with trailers are tested as a rigid combination in a wind tunnel or CFD simulation on occasion, and similar overall aero coefficients are reported.
#
#The commanded wind speed may be overwritten with the VS Command
#
#WIND_SPEED_CONSTANT.
#
#The commanded aero sideslip angle may be overwritten with the VS Command
#
#BETA_REQ.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

